    "body": "## Summary\n\nCloses ADR-033 by flipping status to Implemented, adding an Implementation section that records the measured validation of the spec's zero-visible-delta prediction, and appending a Post-ADR-033 note to ADR-031 (float v1) recording no interaction. **Documentation only — no code changes.**\n\n## The measured validation\n\nADR-033's spec made an explicit honest prediction: **zero visible delta on Wikipedia at desktop 1774**. The pre-merge check confirmed it:\n\n```\ncmp -s /tmp/wiki-adr032-final.png /tmp/wiki-post-adr033.png\n-> PNGs are BYTE-IDENTICAL\n```\n\n**Byte-identical PNG before and after.** The prediction was correct, to the byte.\n\nThis is the **first ADR in the entire arc where the visual prediction was fully validated to the byte.**\n\n## The arc's five correction patterns\n\n| ADR | Pattern | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| 029 | Prediction wrong mid-cycle | Two-stage measurement caught regression, fixed in Commit 3 pre-merge |\n| 030 | Actuals exceeded predictions | Toolbar 21 vs 40-60; grid moved 23px unmodeled |\n| 031 | Predicted \"known overlap\" that didn't exist | Misreading caught by ADR-032's diagnostic, record corrected |\n| 032 | Negative result | Paint culling shipped; did not fix what turned out to be a misread |\n| **033** | **Prediction validated to the byte** | **Zero visible delta confirmed by byte-identical PNG** |\n\nAll five patterns are in the permanent record. All are honest. The arc's actual contribution is this demonstrably honest historical record — the correction patterns are documented alongside the original claims.\n\n## What the Implementation section records\n\n**Structural value (independent of zero visible delta):**\n\n1. **Position infrastructure exists** — before ADR-033, the `position` property was completely unhandled; elements with `position: relative | fixed | absolute | sticky` all participated in normal block flow. Now parsed, stored, and honored for `fixed`.\n\n2. **Principled code path for the 3 fixed elements** in Wikipedia's CSS — currently they leak into block flow; after this ADR they're out-of-flow with viewport anchoring.\n\n3. **Prep for ADR-034 (`position: absolute`)** — the search icon (`span.cdx-text-input__icon` at `top=50% left=9px`) gets proper containing-block anchoring. That's where the first real visible delta from the position arc lands.\n\n4. **Prep for `z-index`** — stacking contexts require position.\n\n## v1 limitations shipped (documented)\n\n- `right` / `bottom` for fixed — unused in Wikipedia's CSS (all 3 rules use `top:12px; left:12px`)\n- No scroll interaction for fixed — anchored to initial viewport top-left\n- `absolute` / `sticky` treated as `static` — needs containing-block tracking (ADR-034) and scroll-aware layout (ADR-034+)\n- No `z-index` for fixed — fixed elements paint at tree position\n\n## What changed\n\n- `docs/decisions/033-position-relative-fixed.md` — Status: Accepted → **Implemented**; new Implementation section (106 lines) leading with byte-identical PNG confirmation\n- `docs/decisions/031-float-layout.md` — Post-ADR-033 note confirming float v1 unaffected\n- `CHANGELOG.md` — new `### Added` entry for ADR-033\n\n## What didn't change\n\n- Zero code changes\n- Test count: 421 cases / 1737 assertions\n- Full suite green\n- No behavior change to main\n\n## The natural next cycle\n\n**ADR-034 (`position: absolute` + containing-block tracking)** is the natural next step — the first position ADR with a real visible driver (search icon at `top=50% left=9px`). Fresh measurement cycle, ~150-200 lines.\n\nRefs #174 #175\n",
